<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The "Number trend" entry in the widget picker - M15.6d, the second of two.

  The cell sizes match habit_grid_widget_info.xml deliberately: the two widgets are siblings and
  should drop onto a home screen at the same size, so a user placing both gets a matched pair rather
  than two cards that need resizing to line up. Three cells was the user's own call at M15.6b - four
  came out just over half the width of their phone, so two widgets could not sit side by side.

  minWidth/minHeight are the pre-31 fallback for targetCellWidth/Height and must stay in agreement
  with them.

  ⚠ resizeMode is both ways, and here it earns it more directly than on the grid: a sparkline has no
  natural height, so it simply fills whatever it is given. A taller widget is a taller curve.

  initialLayout is Glance's own loading layout - what shows between the widget being dropped and
  provideGlance returning.

  ⚠⚠ STILL NO previewImage OR previewLayout, AND THAT IS NOW A DECISION - M15.9, the same one
  habit_grid_widget_info.xml records. MeasureWidget.providePreview composes the real
  MeasureWidgetBody over a sample series, so the picker draws the widget rather than a picture of it.

  ⭐ The old comment's closing claim was right and is now discharged: the picker showing a preview IS
  the whole reason these are two entries rather than one, and until M15.9 both entries drew the same
  fallback icon. ⚠ A drawable could never have finished the job here - this widget's badge prints a
  NUMBER, and a vector has no text.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:configure="com.cristianprincipi.habits.feature.widget.MeasureWidgetConfigActivity"
    android:description="@string/widget_measure_description"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/glance_default_loading_layout"
    android:minHeight="80dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="80dp"
    android:minResizeWidth="110dp"
    android:minWidth="110dp"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:targetCellHeight="2"
    android:targetCellWidth="3"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen" />
